# L §5.16 Closed forms: share of a normal fact is computed from its cdf, which "needs to" (table, L §7.3); with no
# to on the query it is refused. The fact's family is known only from its row, so the check is the run's, made where
# the value is read, in load's words: RUN-DOMAIN (L §8.4 Load refuses what load sees; tally 2.1.8 §4, #162). 2.1.7's
# refcore printed LOAD-TO at run, refusing the reality.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input z: dist
input u01: dist
input u4: dist
input cnt: dist
input q25: num
input two: num
input lvl: num

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  z = normal(0, 1) to 1e-9
  u01 = uniform(0, 1) to 0.001
  u4 = uniform(0, 4) to 0.001
  cnt = binomial(4, 0.5)
  q25 = 0.25
  two = 2
  lvl = 0.5

ask a: share(z <= lvl) law 2026-06-30
=== expect
a: refused: RUN-DOMAIN share of normal needs to u (a cdf of normal needs to)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
warning: WARN-UNREAD input cnt is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input q25 is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input two is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input u01 is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input u4 is read by nothing
